ed systems for surveillance of HIV infection and morbidity in the US</article-title><source>Public Health Rep</source><year>2007</year><volume>122</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>3</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17354520</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Department of Health and Human Services</collab></person-group><article-title>Surveillance of HIV/AIDS related events among persons not receiving care</article-title><source>Federal Register</source><year>2005</year><volume>70</volume><fpage>38152</fpage><lpage>38157</lpage></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>